# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Neither of the two secrets below falls back in production any more. The
# fallbacks used to be in the source, which is public, so a deploy that lost its
# environment came up looking healthy while signing with a key anyone can read.
# `npm run dev` still falls back so a fresh clone runs, and says so on the way past.
#
# They fail at different moments, and the difference matters when you are
# reading a log:
#   PAYLOAD_SECRET   — read as the config loads, so the process will not start.
#   PREVIEW_SECRET   — read when the preview endpoint is used, so the site starts
#                      and serves normally; pressing Preview in the admin is what
#                      fails. Deliberate: the static export builds with
#                      NODE_ENV=production and has no preview endpoint at all.

# Signs Payload's admin sessions, and the cookie that unlocks the private half of
# /about. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# Where the site is served from. Used for preview links and CORS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Guards the draft-preview endpoint. Read when the endpoint is used, so the static
# export — which has no such endpoint — does not need it.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 24
PREVIEW_SECRET=

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local file (default) — back up by copying data/site.db
DATABASE_URI=file:./data/site.db
# Or a hosted libSQL/Turso database for serverless production:
# DATABASE_URI=libsql://your-db.turso.io
# DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Media storage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty for local disk (development only — uploads written next to the
# app do not survive a redeploy on most hosts).
#
# Exactly three of these switch storage over: S3_BUCKET, S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID and
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY. If all three are set, every upload goes to S3-compatible
# object storage (Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, AWS S3) and the rest are optional:
#
#   S3_ENDPOINT    — required by R2 and B2, omitted for AWS S3, which infers it.
#   S3_REGION      — defaults to `auto`, which is what R2 wants.
#   S3_PUBLIC_URL  — NOT passed to the storage plugin. It is read by
#                    next.config.ts, to allow that hostname in next/image. Set it
#                    or images from the bucket will be refused by the optimizer.
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_REGION=auto
# Public base URL of the bucket, used to allow the host in next/image.
S3_PUBLIC_URL=

# ── Email ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No email adapter is configured. Payload says so on every start, and it means
# password-reset messages are written to the server log instead of being sent.
# Recoverable — the link is in the log — but worth knowing before you need it.
# See https://payloadcms.com/docs/email/overview

# ── First run ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used once by `npm run seed` to create the owner account.
SEED_EMAIL=you@example.com
SEED_PASSWORD=

# ── GitHub Pages preview (optional; only read by scripts/build-static.mjs) ────
# Empty for a custom domain. `/personal-site` when serving from the bare
# GitHub project URL, because everything then lives one directory down.
# Baked into the client bundles at build time, so changing it needs a rebuild.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=
# Written to out/CNAME when set. Leave empty until the DNS record exists.
PAGES_CNAME=
